.TH MEM 1
.SH NAME
mem \- memory, processes, CPUs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mem
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mem
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It prints the memory in KiB (total, used, free), then the number of
processes, threads and processors, from the kernel
.RB ( sys_info (2)).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR uptime (1)
